# Local-only evals (may derive from private deal data — never commit)
evals-local/

# Office lock/owner files. Excel writes `~$<name>.xlsx` beside any workbook it
# opens, and that file embeds the OPENER'S REAL NAME. They appear in
# fixtures/ the moment anyone double-clicks a test workbook, and a wildcard
# stage would put a real name into public history. privacy_guard.py cannot
# save us here: it reports clean while the file is merely untracked.
~$*
.~lock.*#

# cowork-harness `critique --out` reports. Run OUTPUT, not source: they embed the
# run's host paths (/Users/..., /var/folders/...) and the graded run's transcript
# excerpts. Keep them out of history the same way runs/ is kept out — a wildcard
# stage would otherwise put a host path into a public commit. privacy_guard.py
# does not flag them (its path class is not in the tree scan).
cowork-tests/*-critique.json
